
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# <type>(#<task>): this commit <verb> <contextual description>
#
#   e.g.  feature(#42): this commit introduces table session checkout
#         fix(#17): this commit prevents duplicate items in an order
#         feature(#30)!: this commit changes the order contract        (breaking)
#         refactor(#8): this commit simplifies the order total handling
#         chore(#00): this commit introduces base repository config files
#
# Then, after a blank line, an optional body: what changed and WHY
# (not how). Wrap at ~72 columns.
#
# ── style ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   - the summary always starts with "this commit <verb> ..."
#       (introduces / refactors / removes / updates / fixes / prevents …)
#   - stay CONTEXTUAL: describe the effect / intent, not the implementation
#   - never name classes, methods, variables or file names in the summary
#   - all lowercase, english, no trailing period
#
# ── types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feature   new functionality                 -> bumps MINOR   (0.X.0)
#   fix       bug fix                            -> bumps PATCH   (0.0.X)
#   feature!  breaking change — put "!" before   -> bumps MAJOR   (X.0.0)
#             the colon:  feature(#42)!: ...
#
#   chore     tooling / config / meta           -> no version bump
#   docs      documentation only                -> no version bump
#   refactor  code change, no behavior change    -> no version bump
#   test      tests only                         -> no version bump
#   style     formatting only (no code change)   -> no version bump
#   perf      performance improvement            -> no version bump
#   ci        pipelines / workflows              -> no version bump
#
# ── rules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   - <task> is numeric (e.g. #42); use #00 when there is no task
#   - only feature / fix / feature! change the version (see GitVersion.yml)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
